text:
- It writes receipt lines to `--receipt <path>`: ndjson, one `write_all` per line, every line `"v":1` + a kebab `kind`. The kinds are:
  - `start` {`cli_version`}: in interactive mode written after the fake agent has taken its `HostTerminal` raw-mode guard on its own stdin/stdout (as the real CLI sets raw mode itself), so tests send no key before it; print mode takes no raw-mode guard and writes it before its four fixture events
  - `size` {`cols`, `rows`}: at start and again whenever the terminal size changed (the resize oracle) — in interactive mode a watcher thread writes the size at once, then polls it every 10 ms and writes on every change, so a resize reaches the receipt with no key after it; nothing while stdin/stdout is not a terminal, and print mode writes none
  - `cwd` {`cwd`}
  - `hold` {`pid`}: the `--exit-no-eof` holder, at its start
  - `env` {`names`}: sorted, names only, never a value
  - `fds` {`fds`}: Unix only
  - `key` {`hex`}: one per byte outside a paste
  - `prompt` {`text`, `hex`, `bare_esc`, `origin` `human`|`harness`, `submit` `fired`|`suppressed`|`local-command`|`no-fixture`|`no-hooks`}
  - `hook` {`event`, `command_absolute`, `ran`, plus `exit_code`, `stderr_len`, `stdout_hex` and `stdin_hex` (the exact bytes offered on the hook's stdin) when it ran, and `spawn_os_error` when the spawn of an absolute `command` failed: the raw OS error as an integer, `null` when the OS gives none}
  - `statusline` {the `hook` kind's fields without `event`}; tests wait for it through `tests/support/fake.rs` `wait_statusline`
  - `step` {`index`, `event`}

- Today the walk (`tests/contract_fixture_hygiene.rs`) covers `fixtures/fake-scripts/*.json` against `schemas/fake-script.v1.json` (draft 2020-12, unknown fields allowed, `v` const 1, closed nine-event enum). The walk covers one or more committed scripts (`fixtures/fake-scripts/{gated-turn,path3,path4,path4-permission}.json` today).
 It also covers the `fixtures/claude/*/*.json` hook payloads (today the sets `2.1.283`, `2.1.287`, `2.1.288` and `2.1.302`: the four spine `{SessionStart,UserPromptSubmit,Stop,SessionEnd}.default.json` in each, `2.1.287`'s four superseded relayed dialog fixtures, the 12 recorded dialog variants `<Event>.<stem>-<digits>.json` under each of `2.1.287`, `2.1.288` and `2.1.302`, the six recorded framing variants of each of `2.1.287` and `2.1.302`, `UserPromptSubmit.paste-1.json`, `UserPromptSubmit.paste-2.json`, `UserPromptSubmit.paste-3.json`, `SessionStart.compact-1.json`, `SessionEnd.clear-1.json` and `SessionStart.clear-1.json`, and the one recorded resume variant of each of `2.1.287` and `2.1.302`, `SessionStart.resume-1.json`, walked by `claude_resume_variants_are_walked_for_every_resume_set`) against `schemas/claude-fixture.v1.json` (tolerant, `required: [hook_event_name]`, its enum the fake agent's nine `REGISTERED_EVENTS`); the two status line variants of each of `2.1.287` and `2.1.302`, `StatusLine.default-1.json` and `StatusLine.rate-limits-1.json`, against `schemas/claude-statusline-fixture.v1.json` (a tolerant object, `session_id` required as a string; `rate_limits`, when present, an object requiring `five_hour` and `seven_day` objects), with the same path, username and email walk (`statusline_variants_are_walked_for_every_statusline_set`, planted status line cases proving each class red); the one agents fixture of each of `2.1.287` and `2.1.302`, `Agents.recorded-1.json`, against `schemas/claude-agents-fixture.v1.json` (one array of rows over the measured keys) with the same walk (`agents_fixtures_pass_hygiene`; planted `planted_clean_agents_read_passes`, `planted_agents_schema_violation_is_rejected`, `planted_agents_absolute_path_is_rejected`, `planted_agents_username_is_rejected`; chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board);
 the one MCP exchange of `2.1.302`, `Mcp.tools-list-1.json`, against `schemas/claude-mcp-fixture.v1.json` (`v` const 1; `client` JSON-RPC 2.0 frames that contain a `tools/list` request with an `id`; `results` keyed by method, `tools/list` holding a `tools` array of named tools) with the same path, username and email walk (`mcp_fixtures_pass_hygiene`; planted `planted_clean_mcp_exchange_passes`, `planted_dirty_mcp_exchange_is_rejected`, `planted_mcp_schema_violation_is_rejected`); and apart from them the `Screen.{modal,ready,turn}.json` screens of `2.1.287`, `2.1.288` and `2.1.302` against `schemas/claude-screen.v1.json` (`screen_phase` modal|ready|turn, `cols` const 80, exactly 24 `rows`); a planted drive-path file proves it red, and a planted nested-path variant proves the variant walk red.
